concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-45 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "45 After section 18 of the Principal Act the following sections are"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-45 ;
    values:originalText "inserted: Appointment etc. of Associate Director \"18A. (1) The Associate Director must be appointed by the Governor-General. \"(2) The Associate Director holds office for the period, not longer than 7 years, specified in the instrument of appointment, but is eligible for re-appointment.  Crimes Legislation Amendment No. 28, 1991 \"(3) A person must not be appointed as the Associate Director unless he or she is a legal practitioner and has been a legal practitioner for at least 5 years. \"(4) A person who has turned 65 must not be appointed as the Associate Director and a person must not be appointed for a period that ends after the day on which the person will turn 65. \"(5) The Associate Director holds office on such terms and conditions (if any) in respect of matters not provided for by this Act as are determined by the Governor-General. Exercise of powers and functions by Associate Director \"18B. (1) Subject to any directions of the Director, the Associate Director has all the powers and functions of the Director, except the Director's powers of delegation under section 31. \"(2) A power or function that is exercised or performed by the Associate Director is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been exercised or performed by the Director. \"(3) Where, under this Act, the exercise of a power or performance of a function by the Director depends on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the Director in relation to a matter, the power or function may be exercised or performed by the Associate Director depending on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the Associate Director in relation to that matter.\". Remuneration and allowances" ;
    skos:definition "inserted: Appointment etc. of Associate Director \"18A. (1) The Associate Director must be appointed by the Governor-General. \"(2) The Associate Director holds office for the period, not longer than 7 years, specified in the instrument of appointment, but is eligible for re-appointment.  Crimes Legislation Amendment No. 28, 1991 \"(3) A person must not be appointed as the Associate Director unless he or she is a legal practitioner and has been a legal practitioner for at least 5 years. \"(4) A person who has turned 65 must not be appointed as the Associate Director and a person must not be appointed for a period that ends after the day on which the person will turn 65. \"(5) The Associate Director holds office on such terms and conditions (if any) in respect of matters not provided for by this Act as are determined by the Governor-General. Exercise of powers and functions by Associate Director \"18B. (1) Subject to any directions of the Director, the Associate Director has all the powers and functions of the Director, except the Director's powers of delegation under section 31. \"(2) A power or function that is exercised or performed by the Associate Director is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been exercised or performed by the Director. \"(3) Where, under this Act, the exercise of a power or performance of a function by the Director depends on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the Director in relation to a matter, the power or function may be exercised or performed by the Associate Director depending on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the Associate Director in relation to that matter.\". Remuneration and allowances"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2f8a022dce9955e5da057323733ce6b71f18278f75f9f62161c844b14105473f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Appointment requirements for Associate Director" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf, p.16" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-45-norm .
