concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-58 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "58 Section 58"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-58 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Section 4 of the Principal Act is amended: (a) by inserting \"Australian Capital Territory and the\" after \"includes the\" in the definition of \"State\" in subsection (1); (b) by inserting \"Australian Capital Territory or the\" after \"include the\" in the definition of \"Territory\" in subsection (1). (2) Despite subsection (1), where, immediately before the commencing day: (a) an order or warrant under the Principal Act was in force; or (b) an application for such an order or warrant had been made but not finally dealt with; and the indictable offence (or alleged or suspected indictable offence) concerned was an offence against a law of the Australian Capital Territory, the Principal Act continues to apply, on and after that day, in relation to: (c) the order, warrant or application; and (d) the offence, or alleged or suspected offence; and (e) any person convicted of the offence, or any person alleged to have committed it or suspected of having committed it; as if subsection (1) had not been enacted. (3) Despite subsection (1), Part VI of the Principal Act continues to apply, on and after the commencing day, in relation to interstate restraining orders and interstate forfeiture orders registered in the Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory before that day as  Crimes Legislation Amendment No. 28, 1991 if references in that Part to a Territory included the Australian Capital Territory. (4) In this section: \"commencing day\" means the day on which this section commences. Charge on property subject to restraining order" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Section 4 of the Principal Act is amended: (a) by inserting \"Australian Capital Territory and the\" after \"includes the\" in the definition of \"State\" in subsection (1); (b) by inserting \"Australian Capital Territory or the\" after \"include the\" in the definition of \"Territory\" in subsection (1). (2) Despite subsection (1), where, immediately before the commencing day: (a) an order or warrant under the Principal Act was in force; or (b) an application for such an order or warrant had been made but not finally dealt with; and the indictable offence (or alleged or suspected indictable offence) concerned was an offence against a law of the Australian Capital Territory, the Principal Act continues to apply, on and after that day, in relation to: (c) the order, warrant or application; and (d) the offence, or alleged or suspected offence; and (e) any person convicted of the offence, or any person alleged to have committed it or suspected of having committed it; as if subsection (1) had not been enacted. (3) Despite subsection (1), Part VI of the Principal Act continues to apply, on and after the commencing day, in relation to interstate restraining orders and interstate forfeiture orders registered in the Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory before that day as  Crimes Legislation Amendment No. 28, 1991 if references in that Part to a Territory included the Australian Capital Territory. (4) In this section: \"commencing day\" means the day on which this section commences. Charge on property subject to restraining order"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5c858b99fbcb1c7eaa424f08afd544a3c3d5c1b332505c11a444cb44b6cfb810" ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-58-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-58-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-58-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991-sec-58-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-act-1991.pdf, p.20" .
